th typical infectious leukocytosis"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts on peripheral smear"]}, "other_mass": 0.0, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers or time-critical syndrome patterns are present. The patient’s vital signs are stable (BP 122/90 mmHg, HR 84/min, O2 99%), and there is no evidence of airway compromise, shock, or herniation risk. Constitutional symptoms and pancytopenia with blasts suggest a hematological process but do not require urgent stabilization before diagnostic refinement.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch B3.1 (CML) has posterior 0.351 < 0.75 and dangerous alternatives B1 (0.083 posterior, danger 0.9) and B2 (0.266 posterior, danger 0.9) remain unresolved. Required discriminators (bone marrow biopsy, flow cytometry) have not yet been performed."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.85, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.35140172487823407, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Multiple myeloma', 'Myelofibrosis'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": true, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B3", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.426}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B3.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML)", "posterior": 0.351, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 3, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "The subacute time course is inconsistent with classic CML (B3.1) but aligns with acute myeloid neop